voice-to-text (2.3.11) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(hotkey): a KeyRelease is never discarded, so the microphone can no
    longer be left recording with the key already up. The press handler
    waited for the previous transcription to finish typing on the same
    thread that delivers KeyRelease, so a real release queued behind it,
    arrived ~0ms after the recording start, and was thrown away as an
    auto-repeat artefact. The wait now runs off the event thread, a release
    always stops the recording, and a watchdog force-stops any hold that
    outlives the buffer cap.
  * fix(audio): a quick tap is no longer reported as a dead microphone. A tap
    can end before the first audio callback fires, and any zero-sample
    capture was diagnosed as a dead stream regardless of how long the key was
    held — leaving a red error icon in the tray and re-opening the capture
    stream for nothing. The hold is now timed from the press, so a genuinely
    dead device is still detected while a hasty tap is simply discarded.
  * fix(hotkey): the Customize Hotkey dialog refuses keys you type with.
    Push-to-talk holds its key globally, so binding space or a letter removed
    that character from every application and fired a recording on each
    press. Printable keys and the editing keys are now rejected with an
    explanation, and startup warns when an existing settings.conf already
    carries one.

 -- Emmanuel Powell-Clark <emmanuel@powellclark.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:13:44 +0100

voice-to-text (2.3.10) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(clipboard): "Copy last transcription" now holds the X11/Wayland
    clipboard selection itself (via xclip/xsel, or wl-copy on Wayland) so the
    copied text survives after the copy without a running clipboard manager. It
    had silently become a no-op for users not running CopyQ or similar, because
    arboard released the selection the moment it was set (FEAT-VTT038
    regression).
  * feat(tray): new "Re-transcribe last recording" menu item re-runs
    transcription on the newest recording and re-types the result — a recovery
    net for when typed output is lost (wrong window focused, target app
    discarded the input, or the typing path failed).
  * feat(cli): --file/-f batch-transcribes a 16 kHz WAV to stdout and exits,
    with clean pipes and exit codes (no tray, no hotkey).
  * feat(audio): honour the selected input-device index when opening the
    capture stream, with fallback to the default device.
  * fix(security): model downloads now hard-fail on a SHA-256 mismatch instead
    of using the corrupt file.
  * fix(macos): the paste-fallback shortcut sends Cmd+V rather than Ctrl+V.
  * fix(reliability): coredump capture plus an FFI/unsafe audit hardening pass.
  * fix(deps): rustls-webpki bumped to 0.103.13 (closes RUSTSEC-2026-0104).

 -- Emmanuel Powell-Clark <emmanuel@powellclark.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 10:56:34 +0100

voice-to-text (2.3.9) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(audio): self-healing capture stream. vtt held one audio capture
    stream open from startup forever; if the mic re-enumerated (USB
    re-plug), the audio session restarted (logout/login), or
    PipeWire/WirePlumber suspended the source, every recording came back
    with zero samples until vtt was manually restarted. A stream error
    now flags it dead and the next recording re-opens it against the
    current default device; any zero-sample capture re-opens the stream
    so the following press works (TASK-VTT121).
  * fix(audio): a zero-sample capture is reported honestly as "No audio
    captured — check microphone" (tray status, error icon, and a desktop
    notification) instead of the misleading "Recording too short (0.00s)".
  * fix(service): the systemd unit uses Restart=always (was on-failure,
    which missed clean-but-wrong exits) and tray Quit now stops the unit
    via systemctl --user stop vtt, so an intentional quit stays quit
    instead of fighting the restart policy (TASK-VTT122).
  * feat: correction dictionary — a user-editable list of
    misheard -> correct word/phrase pairs in settings.conf, applied
    deterministically after transcription to fix recurring
    mistranscriptions (names, jargon) that initial_prompt bias alone
    cannot pin down (TASK-VTT118).
  * security: anyhow bumped 1.0.102 -> 1.0.103 (RUSTSEC-2026-0190).

 -- Emmanuel Powell-Clark <emmanuel@powellclark.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 04:54:50 +0100

voice-to-text (2.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(typing): switch from enigo Key::Unicode to xdotool type
    --clearmodifiers — eliminates dropped sentence-starter characters
    (I, T, Y, C) caused by an XKB keysym remap race condition.
    Adds xdotool to package Depends; falls back to enigo if missing.
  * fix(typing): keystroke delay tuned (4ms → 12ms → 20ms, landed at
    12ms with xdotool) to stop letter drops on slower X servers.
  * fix(debian): postinst try-restarts vtt-linux on apt upgrade so
    the new binary actually runs instead of leaving the old one
    resident until next login.
  * fix(debian): postrm message points at v2.0 cache paths, not v1.x.
  * fix(debian): copyright points at vtt-linux.prebuilt, not the
    excluded third_party/ directory; drop redundant
    DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS export to silence lintian.
  * feat(cli): --version / -V and --help / -h flags. Exit cleanly
    before singleton-lock and GTK init so users can confirm what's
    installed without launching the tray.
  * feat(main): singleton-lock error reports the holding PID with a
    ready-to-paste kill command, instead of a bare "already running".
  * feat(main): worker-thread death is surfaced to the user via
    notify-send instead of being silently dropped.
  * feat(audio): helpful error message when no default input device
    is configured, pointing at pavucontrol.
  * feat(main): version logged on startup for easier issue triage.
  * fix(tray): hotkey capture and press-event both reject keycodes
    > 255 with a clear message, instead of silently truncating.
  * fix(tray): About dialog says "Hold and release" rather than
    "start/stop" — matches actual push-to-talk behaviour.
  * refactor(tray): model menu derived from the MODELS catalogue
    instead of a hardcoded list, so adding a model in models.rs is
    enough to wire it into the UI.
  * refactor(models): resolve_variant's .en check is derived from
    MODELS rather than hardcoded.
  * perf(main): singleton_lock runs before logging::init so failed
    start attempts no longer pollute the daily log.
  * chore(service): drop stale PYTHONPATH from vtt.service, pass
    XDG_SESSION_TYPE for Wayland/X11 detection.
  * chore(deps): remove unused gdk dependency.
  * internal: GitHub Actions CI with cargo audit, 63+ unit tests
    (audio, settings, models, tray, logging, hotkey, transcribe),
    pre-push hook, ADR-0004 lightweight regression testing,
    SECURITY.md, dead-code cleanup, lintian fixes, Cargo.lock v3
    guard in release-ppa.sh.

