voice-to-text (2.0.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix: switch to pre-built binary distribution on the PPA.
    Ubuntu LTS cargo 1.75 cannot parse edition-2024 Cargo.toml manifests
    that modern Rust deps use (getrandom 0.3, moxcms, pxfm, toml_edit
    via cpal and arboard). Both 2.0.0 and 2.0.1 failed to build on
    Launchpad for this reason.
  * debian/rules now installs vtt-linux.prebuilt instead of running
    cargo. The binary is compiled locally with Rust 1.91 and committed.
  * Build-Depends reduced to debhelper-compat (= 13) plus runtime libs
    needed by dh_shlibdeps.
  * Source tarball reduced dramatically (vendor/ no longer shipped).
  * Remove notify-rust crate; notifications now shell to notify-send
    from libnotify-bin (added to Depends).
  * When Ubuntu eventually ships rustc 1.85+, this file can revert to
    the cargo-build path at git commit efa5d75.

