voice-to-text (2.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Rust binary now shipped — 1.0.x releases installed the legacy C binary
    despite the Rust rewrite being in the tree since 1.0.16
  * whisper-rs in-process replaces the CT2 + Python subprocess path — the
    model loads once at startup and remains resident for sub-second
    transcriptions regardless of clip length or model size
  * Python runtime dependency removed (no more python3, python3-pip,
    faster-whisper, or ctranslate2 in the install footprint)
  * Vulkan GPU acceleration on Linux works universally with NVIDIA, AMD,
    and Intel GPUs without requiring the CUDA Toolkit
  * Model menu simplified to a flat list: Small, Medium, Large-v3-turbo,
    Large-v3 — the W/CT2 prefixes are retired along with the dead backends
  * Default model ggml-small.en.bin downloaded via postinst on first install
  * GGML models downloaded on demand from ggerganov/whisper.cpp when users
    select alternatives from the tray menu
  * Breaking: existing CT2 model caches at ~/.cache/huggingface/ are no
    longer used; GGML models re-download on first selection
  * Delete 7,638 lines of obsolete C and Objective-C source
  * See ADR-0003 at CONSCIOUSNESS/adr/0003-*.md for the full architectural
    decision record

